1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,150
Two nights before the Manchester derby…

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,650
Mario Balotelli’s bathroom caught fire.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,650
Fireworks.

4
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,250
October 2011.

5
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:11,350
Just after midnight, a firework set the bathroom of his rented house alight.

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,350
Two fire engines came. Nobody was hurt.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,950
The repair bill? Reportedly… £400,000.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,450
And Mario? He blamed a friend.

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,250
Then, on Sunday… Manchester City went to Old Trafford.

10
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,850
22 minutes in, Balotelli scores.

11
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:28,750
And he lifts his shirt.

12
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,150
Underneath, a message: Why always me?

13
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,850
He scored again after the break.

14
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,850
City won… six goals to one. At Old Trafford.

15
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,950
United’s worst home defeat in 56 years.

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,450
Sir Alex Ferguson called it… “our worst ever day.”

17
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,150
And the funniest part?

18
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,350
Days later, Mario became the face of a firework safety campaign.

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,350
Genius… or chaos?

20
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,350
Tell me in the comments.
